      "body": "## Summary\n\n- The benchmark chart and the embodied README list Pi0.5 at 2.80x, while the\n  published blog post reports 2.63x (bf16) and 3.00x (bf16 + TorchAO FP8).\n  Readers comparing the two sources see a number that matches neither.\n- Align the documented figure with the published 3.00x result.\n\n## Changes\n\n- `docs/assets/images/benchmark_image.py`: Pi0.5 row 2.80 -> 3.00\n- `docs/assets/images/benchmark_speedup.png`: regenerated from the script above\n- `loongforge/embodied/README.md`, `README_zh.md`: performance table 2.80x -> 3.00x\n\nRow ordering is unchanged in both the chart and the tables — Pi0.5 stays second\nbehind DreamZero (4.38x), and the accent bar stays on DeepSeek-V3.2 Lite (5.04x).\n\n## Test Plan\n\n- Regenerated the PNG with `python docs/assets/images/benchmark_image.py`\n  (matplotlib 3.10.7, Inter 4.1) and confirmed only the Pi0.5 bar and its label\n  changed; the remaining pixel differences are text antialiasing from a\n  different Inter/matplotlib build than the one that produced the committed PNG.\n- `pre-commit run --files <changed files>`: all hooks pass.\n\nSource for the number:\nhttps://baidu-baige.github.io/LoongForge/blog/2026-10-loongforge-pi05-3x-training-acceleration.html\n",
